6</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/eurpub/8.2.176</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Agyemang</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Redekop</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name><name><surname>Owusu-Dabo</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruijnzeels</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Blood pressure patterns in rural, semi-urban and urban children in Ashanti region of Ghana, West Africa</article-title><source>BMC Public Health</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>114</fpage><comment>doi:10.1186/1471-2458-5-114</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16262905</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2458-5-114</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Obika</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>Adedoyin</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Olowoyeye</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pattern of paediatric blood pressure in rural, semi-urban and urban communities in Ilorin, Nigeria</article-title><source>Afr J Med Med Sci</source><year>1995</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>371</fpage><lpage>377</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8886153</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pearson</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cardiovascular disease in developing countries: myths, realities and opportunities</article-title><source>Card Drugs Therapy</source><year>1999</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1007727924276</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balogun</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Obajuluwa</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Olaogun</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name><name><surname>Abereoje</surname><given-names>OK</given-names></name><name><surname>Oyeyemi</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name><name><surname>Adeolu</surname><given-names>OO</given-names></name><name><surname>Balogun</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of parental socioeconomic status on casual blood pressure of Nigerian school children</article-title><source>Int J Cardiology</source><year>1990</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>69</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0167-5273(90)90274-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rotimi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ataman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>The prevalence of hypertension in seven populations of West African Origin</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><year>1997</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>160</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9103091</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2105/AJPH.87.2.160</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sugiyama</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Xie</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Graham-Maar</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Inoue</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Stettler</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dietary and Lifestyle Factors Associated with Blood Pressure among U.S. Adolescents</article-title><source>Journal of Adolescent Health</source><year>2006</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>166</fpage><lpage>172</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17259057</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jadohealth.2006.09.006</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaufman</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Owoaje</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rotimi</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Determinants of hypertension in West Africa: contribution of anthropometric and dietary factors to urban, rural and socioeconomic gradients</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><year>1996</year><volume>143</volume><fpage>1203</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8651219</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>